# Great Train Heist, third mode ({R} + {R}): "Choose target opponent. Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to
# that player this turn, create a tapped Treasure token" (CR 603.7b, 603.7c). In a game of three, Bot1 casts it on turn 4
# choosing Bot3, then Memnite attacks Bot2 and Bile-Vial Boggart attacks Bot3: both connect (Bot2 19, Bot3 19), but only the
# Boggart's damage was dealt to the chosen player, so there is one tapped Treasure, not two.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Bile-Vial Boggart
Mountain
Great Train Heist
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bile-Vial Boggart.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Great Train Heist.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Choose target opponent)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
[T4 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2; Bile-Vial Boggart > Bot3)
[T4 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot3.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Bile-Vial Boggart; Memnite; Mountain; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Treasure Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Tapped = true
